+## 0. Contract boundary
+
+This contract owns what would prove or disprove the three product promises in `product-contract.md`. It does not select a stack, notification provider, authentication system, or deployment host: none is present in this workspace. The working platform assumption is a browser-based team-facilitator product; it is reversible and must be replaced by the actual distribution shape before implementation validation.
+
+P1 applies: captures become evidence only after a skeptical evaluator records what they tried to break. P2 applies: every pass below requires an observed request, state transition, or datastore read-back. P3 applies: an unreachable control or unavailable service is a logged defect attempt, not a skipped proof. P4 applies: the probe list prompts an independent adversary; it is not a definition of done.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web browser (reversible planning assumption) | Clean production web bundle with its immutable build identifier recorded | Production HTTPS origin — host not yet selected |
+
+No launch platform is currently implemented. A localhost or development-server run can support iteration only and cannot advance a launch readiness claim.
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Platform: Web browser
+
+- A clean production build exercised at the deployed production-like origin, with build SHA, sanitized configuration, browser version, and UTC clock recorded.
+- A real facilitator principal and a second principal in another workspace, executing the primary flow through the UI and observed at the API/datastore boundary.
+- A pre-walk baseline query and post-walk datastore read-back for every reminder, delivery attempt, and terminal delivery status claimed by the walk.
+- A runtime accessibility-tree dump plus measured container/content geometry at 375 px, 768 px, and 1440 px for the action-confirmation and reminder-status views.
+- A separately adjudicated LARP transcript and recording of the built artifact. A screenshot alone is only a capture.
+
