+
+### Promise falsification matrix
+
+| Promise | Falsifying observation | Claim type | Required discharge artifact |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001: no reminder before explicit confirmation of action text, owner, and due date | An incomplete or unconfirmed draft creates a reminder, delivery job, or scheduled timestamp; or changing a field after preview is not what the confirmation commits. | `persistence` | Baseline and post-attempt datastore reads plus the built-flow transcript: `db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-premature-schedule.log` |
+| PRM-002: a workspace cannot read another workspace's transcript, action, or delivery status | A principal from workspace B can list, fetch, search, or mutate workspace A's transcript, action, or delivery status; or workspace A loses its own visibility. | `visibility` | Two real-principal, both-direction reads and forbidden-write attempts: `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-cross-workspace.log` |
+| PRM-003: a confirmed reminder is delivered exactly once or exposes a truthful terminal failure state | One confirmation produces zero delivery records without a terminal status, more than one recipient delivery, a retry that duplicates delivery, or a hidden/false success after provider failure. | `persistence` | Baseline, delivery-provider boundary record, and datastore read-back of one delivery or truthful terminal status: `db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/logs/<sha>-delivery-once-or-terminal.log` |
+
+The paths above are required evidence homes, not evidence already collected. Their `<epic>`, `<story>`, and `<sha>` tokens are naming variables, not launch placeholders.
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+- Development-server, localhost, Storybook-only, or unversioned screenshots cited for UX-RC, SHIP-RC, or SHIP.
+- A mocked scheduler, notification provider, datastore, or authorization client cited for production acceptance, delivery, persistence, or workspace isolation.
+- A bypass-capable principal or a single-principal read cited for PRM-002.
+- A success toast, queue enqueue log, or provider request alone cited for PRM-003; it cannot establish exactly-once delivery or a truthful terminal status.
+- A post-walk datastore read without a baseline cited for a new reminder or delivery.
+- A static assertion that confirmation guards exist cited for PRM-001, or that tenant predicates exist cited for PRM-002.
+- An unadjudicated screenshot, recording, or green test suite cited as evidence of quality or launch readiness.
+
+Any validation report using an invalid source labels the affected claim **Surrogate Proof** and cannot claim UX-RC or higher for that claim.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+| Test | Persona / principal | Failure-path probe and pass condition | Evidence home |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Confirmed action | Facilitator in workspace A | Try blank action text, absent owner, absent/invalid due date, cancel at confirmation, and edit after preview. No attempt may create a reminder or delivery job; a fully confirmed action creates one. | `capture:epics/<epic>/stories/<story>/larp-recordings/<sha>-facilitator-confirmation.md` and `db-catalog:logs/<sha>-premature-schedule.log` |
+| Workspace isolation | Facilitator A and facilitator B in distinct workspaces | Seed A's transcript/action/delivery state; B lists, direct-fetches, searches, and attempts mutation. B sees and changes none; A still sees its own records. | `live-probe:logs/<sha>-cross-workspace.log` |
+| Delivery once or terminal truth | Facilitator A; real delivery transport once selected | Trigger the due boundary twice/concurrently, simulate provider timeout/reject after accepted hand-off, then retry/restart worker. Exactly one completed delivery exists, or one terminal failure visible to A with the recorded cause and no false delivered state. | `db-catalog:logs/<sha>-delivery-once-or-terminal.log`, `capture:transcripts/<sha>-delivery-recovery.md` |
+| Cold-start comprehension and fit | First-time facilitator | From a clean production build, identify the action to take and its confirmation state within five seconds; measure action confirmation and terminal-status views at 375/768/1440 px and inspect the platform AX tree. | `capture:screenshots/<sha>-cold-start-*.png`, `ax-dump:ax-trees/<sha>-confirmation.json`, `capture:transcripts/<sha>-comprehension.md` |
+
+An unavailable delivery transport is a NO-SHIP finding for PRM-003 until the logged attempt and terminal-failure behavior can be exercised.
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Green evidence makes a flow eligible for judgment; it does not establish quality. An independent evaluator scores Functional, Trust, and Comprehension from 0–10 after the LARP. A 9 or 10 requires a distinct skeptical note for that dimension and no active P0/P1; any active P2 caps the affected dimension at 8. Runtime evidence supersedes an older scorecard.
+
+For Pulseboard, Trust is specifically judged by whether the UI distinguishes **draft**, **confirmed**, **delivered**, and **terminal failure** without implying an action happened when it did not. Comprehension is judged by the cold-start probe in §4.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+Every UX-RC-or-higher report records the build SHA, production bundle identifier, sanitized configuration identity, browser/runtime version, screenshots, AX dump, geometry measurements, network/backend logs for boundary calls, and a skeptical LARP verdict. No implementation or project-specific automated gate exists yet; that absence is NO-SHIP, not a waived green gate.
