+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+| Boundary | What proves the boundary when selected | What does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| Authentication and workspace authorization | Real sign-in as A and B against the production security layer, including allowed and forbidden reads/writes. | Mock principals, service-role/bypass reads, or endpoint shape alone. |
+| Reminder persistence and scheduling | Baseline → confirmation attempt → datastore read-back showing the expected state transition and scheduled timestamp only after confirmation. | UI toast, queue log, or post-read without baseline. |
+| Reminder delivery transport | A provider-originated delivery identifier/receipt reconciled to exactly one persisted reminder, or a persisted terminal failure whose cause and time are visible in the product. | A mocked provider, enqueue success, or an unobserved retry. |
+| Observability | A deliberately generated non-sensitive failure reaches the selected error/operational record and correlates to the reminder attempt. | Console output alone. |
+
+No concrete provider is selected in this workspace. Therefore this section specifies future proof obligations and does not claim any real service works.
