+## 8. Readiness State Gate Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence and blocker rule |
+|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Current state. No implementation, selected production distribution, live service, or collected runtime proof exists. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Non-vacuous automated checks cover confirmation preconditions, idempotent delivery state transitions, and workspace boundaries; negative guard mutation makes each guard test red. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | Real authorization, persistence, scheduler, and delivery-boundary round trips meet §2 and §7; schema/datastore read-backs match the deployed build. |
+| UX-RC | Clean production-like browser build passes all §4 LARPs, with cold start, AX/geometry measurements, and separate DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD adjudication. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | If a paid path is introduced, real entitlement/payment acceptance, failure posture, support route, and value-defensibility are recorded; otherwise explicitly n/a in the then-current validation report. |
+| SHIP-RC | Distributed launch build, live configured services, fresh evidence, no active P0/P1, and no surrogate proof for PRM-001–003. |
+| SHIP | Post-deploy smoke repeats each promise’s critical read/write/delivery path and confirms operational health. |
