+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+| Axis / gate | Who records the pass | What can overturn it |
+|---|---|---|
+| CORRECT / IMPL-GREEN | Automated checks plus an independent audit | A failing negative control, mutation, or runtime contradiction |
+| ON-CONTRACT / UX-RC | LARP evaluator | Any promise-matrix falsifier in §2 |
+| FELT-GOOD / UX-RC | Independent LARP evaluator | A skeptical quality note or cold-start/fit failure |
+| TASTE / SHIP-RC | AI evaluator surfaces aesthetic forks; owner resolves direction | Owner decision or severe runtime craft finding |
+| SHIP | Release owner | Failed post-deploy smoke or stale/surrogate evidence |
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+| Probe | Expected behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Bypass confirmation | Missing, blank, malformed, or post-preview-mutated action fields never produce a reminder, schedule, or delivery job. |
+| Duplicate dispatch | Concurrent due triggers, worker restart, and provider timeout cannot produce two completed deliveries. |
+| Provider ambiguity | A provider timeout or reject ends in a visible, truthful terminal state or bounded retry state; never a silent hang or false delivered state. |
+| Cross-workspace enumeration | B cannot infer A’s transcript/action/delivery status through list, search, direct identifier, export, or mutation paths. |
+| Authorization loss mid-flow | Expired/revoked session cannot confirm, schedule, or expose another workspace’s existing state. |
+| Clock boundary | UTC/local timezone and DST boundary runs preserve the confirmed due instant and do not create early, late, or duplicate delivery. |
+| Persistence interruption | Datastore/scheduler failure between confirmation and scheduling leaves an observable non-success state and no orphan delivery. |
+| Cold-start legibility | A first-time facilitator can identify the action, owner, due date, confirmation state, and terminal failure state without being misled by optimistic UI. |
+
+Each probe needs a logged attempt and the required evidence substrate from §2; a green row is not implied by its presence here.
+
